# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep secrets out of it.
# `.env` holds APP_SECRET and the SMTP password — it must never be copied into
# a layer, which is why the runtime reads its configuration from the
# environment instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo

.git
.github
.claude
.dual-graph

*.md
!README.md
docs
schemas

# `clients/agent/bin` holds the binaries `/install.sh` hands out, which CI
# populates. Most stay out of the image: shipping all five cross-compiled
# targets for both tools would add about 39 MB for platforms the container can
# neither run nor usually be asked for, and `routes/download.ts` answers with a
# clear "build it or take one from the releases" when one is absent.
#
# The Linux ones are the exception, for two reasons that the rest do not share:
# the `agent` service in docker-compose.prod.yml executes one of them, and Linux
# is the host an operator is overwhelmingly installing an agent onto — leaving
# it out is what made `/install.sh` answer with the SPA's catch-all HTML on a
# published image, piping a web page into a shell.
clients
!clients/agent/bin/tern-agent-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl
!clients/agent/bin/tern-agent-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl
!clients/agent/bin/tern-proxy-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl
!clients/agent/bin/tern-proxy-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl

**/*.test.ts
**/*.integration.test.ts
